---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 md:px-12 lg:px-24 py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
        Everything you need to know about Process and trauma-informed AI learning tools
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-12">
      <!-- What is Process? -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          What is Process and how is it different from other mental health apps?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            Made by and for people living with complex trauma, ProcessIt is a trauma recovery resource and support tool designed as a supplemental tool to therapy. Unlike generic mental health apps that focus on general anxiety or depression, we address the emotional dysregulation and other challenges specific to complex trauma. We provide trauma-informed support to help you process triggers, understand patterns, and regulate your nervous system—all designed to complement professional therapy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Is this therapy? -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          Is Process a replacement for therapy?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            No, ProcessIt is not a replacement for professional therapy. We're designed as a supplemental tool to therapy that can-
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Support your therapy:</strong> Use insights from ProcessIt to prepare for therapy sessions and access supplemental support between appointments</li>
            <li><strong>Bridge gaps in care:</strong> Provide supplemental support when you can't access therapy or between sessions</li>
            <li><strong>Support the majority of complex trauma survivors who don't have access to trauma-informed resources</strong></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <strong>Think of us as a trauma recovery resource that works alongside your therapy to help you process triggers, track healing, and regulate your nervous system.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            We always encourage users to seek professional mental health care when possible. ProcessIt is designed to supplement and support your therapy journey, not replace professional treatment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Crisis Support -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          What if I'm in crisis?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            Process is not equipped for crisis intervention. If you're experiencing thoughts of self-harm or suicide, please reach out for immediate help:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Emergency Services:</strong> 911</li>
            <li><strong>National Suicide Prevention Lifeline:</strong> 988</li>
            <li><strong>Crisis Text Line:</strong> Text HOME to 741741</li>
            <li><strong>Your local emergency room or crisis center</strong></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Our AI can recognize crisis language and will provide these resources, but we cannot replace emergency mental health services. Your safety is the top priority.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- How does it work? -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          How does Process work?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            ProcessIt provides trauma-informed support through a mobile app. Here's how it works:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Start a conversation:</strong> Share what you're experiencing through text or voice</li>
            <li><strong>Get support:</strong> Receive trauma-informed understanding and compassionate responses</li>
            <li><strong>Build awareness:</strong> Learn about your patterns, triggers, and responses over time</li>
            <li><strong>Continue learning:</strong> Use insights to enhance your understanding and personal growth</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Trauma-Informed AI -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          How is your AI trauma-informed?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            Our AI is specifically designed to support people with complex trauma by:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Trauma-informed frameworks:</strong> Built using trauma-informed principles and developed through lived experience and research—including insights learned through our own healing journeys.</li>
            <li><strong>Safety-first approach:</strong> Always prioritizing your sense of safety before moving into deeper support.</li>
            <li><strong>Complex trauma understanding:</strong> Recognizing the unique challenges of complex trauma and providing support in a way that feels safe and supportive.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pattern Recognition -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          How does Process help me understand my patterns and triggers?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            Through your conversations with our AI, Process helps you explore your experiences. **Advanced pattern recognition and insights are coming soon**, but for now you can discover:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Trigger identification:</strong> Recognizing what situations or thoughts activate your trauma responses</li>
            <li><strong>Response patterns:</strong> Understanding how you typically react to different triggers</li>
            <li><strong>Core beliefs:</strong> Identifying underlying beliefs that influence your responses</li>
            <li><strong>Self-compassion:</strong> Helping you develop new, supportive self-talk and affirmations to nurture your inner child and promote learning.</li>
            <li><strong>Growth tracking:</strong> Monitoring your progress in understanding and managing your responses</li>
            <li><strong>New affirmations:</strong> Personalized affirmations tailored to your learning journey</li>
            <li><strong>Progress celebration:</strong> Acknowledging and celebrating the steps you take toward learning and self-understanding</li>
            <li><strong>Advanced pattern recognition:</strong> Deeper analysis of your triggers, responses, and learning patterns</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-4">
            The goal is to help you develop greater self-awareness and make conscious choices about your responses, supporting your ongoing growth and understanding.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pricing -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          How much does Process cost?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            We believe trauma-informed support should be accessible, so we offer
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Free tier:</strong> Essential learning tools and basic conversations</li>
            <li><strong>Premium tier:</strong> Advanced features and enhanced learning capabilities</li>
            <li>Text and voice conversations for emotional learning</li>
            <li>Basic pattern recognition and self-compassion learning</li>
            <li>Trauma-informed recovery resource</li>
            <li>24/7 availability for learning</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <strong>Free tier:</strong> Text-based conversations for basic emotional learning
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            We're committed to ensuring cost is never a barrier to accessing trauma-informed support. ProcessIt offers a 7-day free trial with full access to all features, then $11.99/month. This supplemental tool to therapy provides support between sessions and helps bridge gaps in care.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <strong>Premium features include:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li>Voice conversations for hands-free learning</li>
            <li>Extended conversation history for deeper insights</li>
            <li>Advanced pattern recognition and analysis</li>
            <li>Build insights: Over time, experience learning, discover patterns, and develop self-regulation skills.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Trust -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          Who built Process and why should I trust it?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            Process is built by trauma survivors, for trauma survivors, grounded in our own lived experience of trauma. We both worked in tech until we realized that supporting others on their learning journey is our true calling and passion. Our work is guided by advisors from the trauma therapy community, ensuring that everything we build is rooted in empathy, understanding, and real-world expertise.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Getting Started -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
          How do I get started with Process?
        </h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg">
          <p class="mb-4">
            Process is now available! You can sign up directly to start your learning journey.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            <strong>Getting started is simple:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Download:</strong> Get ProcessIt from the iOS App Store</li>
            <li><strong>Start your trial:</strong> Begin with a 7-day free trial with full access to all features</li>
            <li><strong>Connect with support:</strong> Use voice or text to share what you're experiencing with your trauma-informed support companion</li>
            <li><strong>Track your healing:</strong> Use the daily tracker and regulation tools to support your recovery journey</li>
            <li><strong>Build insights:</strong> Receive personalized insights about your patterns, triggers, and trauma responses</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question');
    const answers = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-answer');
    const pluses = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-plus');
    const minuses = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-minus');
    let active = null;
    questions.forEach((btn, idx) => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        const id = btn.getAttribute('data-faq');
        answers.forEach((ans, i) => {
          if (ans.getAttribute('data-faq') === id) {
            const isOpen = ans.style.display === 'block';
            ans.style.display = isOpen ? 'none' : 'block';
            pluses[idx].style.display = isOpen ? '' : 'none';
            minuses[idx].style.display = isOpen ? 'none' : '';
          } else {
            ans.style.display = 'none';
            pluses[i].style.display = '';
            minuses[i].style.display = 'none';
          }
        });
      });
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .faq-item {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .faq-item:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>